<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · text</p><h1 class="enc-title">Indian Independence Act 1947</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1947</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Indian Independence Act</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Indian Independence Act 1947 was an act of the British Parliament that partitioned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-india">British India</a> into the two independent <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">dominions</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> from 15 August 1947. It ended British rule and the British monarch's title of Emperor of India and freed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a> from British paramountcy. It was passed in July 1947 under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/clement-attlee">Clement Attlee</a>'s Labour government.</p></div>
